    "title": "How to Watch Louisville Cardinals vs. South Florida Bulls: Live Stream or on TV - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "The No. 6 Louisville Cardinals (23-10) and the No. 11 South Florida Bulls (25-8) battle on Thursday for a spot in the second round of the NCAA Tournament. The first-round matchup begins at 1:30 p.m. ET. In its most recent game, Louisville lost to Miami (FL) on Thursday, 78-73. Ryan Conwell scored a team-high 22 points (and contributed three assists and nine rebounds). On Sunday, in its most recent game, South Florida beat Wichita State 70-55. With 19 points, Wes Enis was its top scorer. When is Louisville vs. South Florida and when does it start? This contest between the Cardinals and Bulls will begin on Thursday, March 19, 2026. You can expect the opening tip at 1:30 p.m. ET. Where to Watch Louisville vs. South Florida The Cardinals and Bulls will take to the floor at KeyBank Center for this matchup on March 19, and if you would like to catch the event live, get your tickets now from Vivid Seats! What channel is the game on? You can catch this game live on TNT. Louisville Cardinals vs. South Florida Bulls Game Preview Louisville Stats, Odds & Insights Louisville outscores opponents by 12.6 points per game (scoring 84.8 per game to rank 19th in college basketball while allowing 72.2 per outing to rank 129th in college basketball) and has a +415 scoring differential overall. The 84.8 points the Cardinals average are 9.3 more than the Bulls concede. Louisville knocks down 11.5 three-pointers per game (fifth-most in college basketball), 3.9 more than its opponents (7.6). It is shooting 35.7% from beyond the arc (85th in college basketball) while allowing opponents to shoot 32.7%. Offensively, the Cardinals have fared better at home this year, scoring 90.9 points per game, compared to 79.5 per game in road games. Louisville has been scoring 82.5 points per contest in its last 10 appearances, an average that’s a little lower than the 84.8 it has scored over the course of the 2025-26 season. South Florida Stats, Odds & Insights South Florida puts up 87.7 points per game (eighth in college basketball) while giving up 75.5 per contest (228th in college basketball). It has a +403 scoring differential and outscores opponents by 12.2 points per game. The Bulls’ 87.7 points per game are 15.5 more than the Cardinals allow. South Florida hits 1.4 more threes per contest than the opposition, 9.6 (45th in college basketball) compared to its opponents’ 8.2. At home the Bulls are putting up 91.5 points per game, 4.8 more than they are averaging away (86.7). South Florida is averaging 81.6 points per contest in its last 10 games, which is 6.1 fewer points than its average for the season (87.7). Cardinals Key Players to Watch Cardinals Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Ryan Conwell 32 18.7 4.8 2.5 1.2 0.2 3.3 Mikel Brown Jr. 21 18.2 3.3 4.7 1.2 0.1 2.6 J’Vonne Hadley 32 11.8 5.2 1.7 1 0.3 1.1 Isaac McKneely 33 10.6 3 1.4 0.5 0.1 2.6 Sananda Fru 33 9.2 6 1.3 0.5 1.4 0.1 Bulls Key Players to Watch Bulls Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Wes Enis 31 16.8 3.6 2.5 1 0.1 3.5 Izaiyah Nelson 33 15.7 9.6 1.2 1.6 1.4 0.2 Joseph Pinion 33 14.2 3.8 2.2 1.6 0.2 3.2 Josh Omojafo 33 11.5 5.3 1.8 0.8 0.2 0.7 CJ Brown 33 11.1 3.9 4.8 1.1 0.3 0.5 And for more CBB game previews, NCAA basketball picks or even how to bet on college basketball check out the latest NCAAB lines on Betsperts.",
